{title: 605 - My Soul, Be on Thy Guard}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #605 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 605}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]My soul, be on they guard!
[Bb]Ten [F]thousand foes [Eb/Bb]arise;
[Bb]The hosts [F]of [Bb]sin are [F/C]pressing [Bb]hard
[Adim]To [Bb]draw thee [Dm/A]from [F]the [Bb/F]skies.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]O watch, and fight, and pray!
[Bb]The [F]battle ne'er [Eb/Bb]give [Dm/A]o'er;
[Bb]Renew [F]it [Bb]boldly every day,
[Adim]And [Bb]help divine [F]implore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Ne'er think the victory won,
[Bb]Nor [F]lay [Bb/F]thine [F]armor [Dm/A]down;
[Bb]Thy arduous task will [F/C]not [Bb]be done
[Adim]Till [Bb]thou obtain [F]the [Bb/F]crown.
{end_of_verse}
